    "gp_section_633407305174090730": {
      "type": "gp-section-633407305174090730",
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "c457ef63739aab4f3d89d46ccfa8dca1c21d3e199e3ecb70cd138eb513413a0d_1_1_1_0__1",
        "ggSpCjA0kdO_background_desktop_image_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0306/4076/7108/files/untitled-436_JKP_SS_square_27e0788f-687c-4bc1-a119-05d3fd865d64.jpg",
        "ggSpCjA0kdO_background_mobile_image_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0306/4076/7108/files/026A4307_feet_close_up_8ed221a1-3b86-497c-ad7c-005e7f3315ce.jpg",
        "ggOBHSyzmRF_text": "Loved By All",
        "ggUfnrowzD4_text": "<p>Parents &amp; Pediatric Feeding Specialists Can't Stop Raving</p>",
        "gg4yoixhjmU_text": "<p>I am in TEARS</p>",
        "ggmIZ3BZL-G_text": "<p>“We've been struggling with solids for a few months. Our daughter was never super engaged or excited about eating. She's always grunting and kicking her legs and just plain looked uncomfortable. I've been feeling so defeated. THIS FOOTREST IS A GAME CHANGER! She devoured her food tonight; I had to give her MORE food. My husband and I honeslty couldn't believe our eyes. There was no resistance, just a happy girl enjoying her pasta.”</p>",
        "ggDWbyLAjm4_text": "<p>Relief for a Stressed Mama</p>",
        "gg6UEoKvLn-_text": "<p>\"This is probably the best thing you can purchase for your IKEA highchair. The quality is amazing. My child went from wanting to be in the highchair for very short periods of time to sitting for an entire meal plus allowing me to finish my meal!\"</p>",
        "ggMMI0RNuxR_text": "<p>OT Approved</p>",
        "gg5RgknMlB8_text": "<p>\"My son is 14 months and has an oral aversion and feeding difficulties. His OT and Speech Therapist both suggested keeping his feet flat for meals, but I couldn't sink the money for a highchair like the Tripp Trapp. Thank goodness for your footrest!!! I'm SO grateful to you for making high quality, useful products at an accessible price for everyone! I'm telling everyone about this footrest and son's OT is already recommending it to her other clients.\"</p>"
      }
    },
    "gp_section_633407305174156266": {
      "type": "gp-section-633407305174156266",
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "2723aa28a52c3de87a0535eccfb7c403ff1a036391991fbab040e236c717203e_1_1_1_0__1",
        "gg_klAMm853_text": "Frequently Asked Questions",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_0": "<p>How do highchair footrests help prevent choking?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_1": "<p>What are signs my baby needs a footrest?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_2": "<p>What is the 90/90/90 rule I keep hearing about?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_3": "<p>Is the YBG footrest fully adjustable?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_4": "<p>What age should use a footrest?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_5": "<p>Do you need tools to install or adjust?&nbsp;</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_6": "<p>How do I position my footrest? What side up? What side facing forward?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_7": "<p>I didn't receive the clamps...what should I do?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_8": "<p>My footrest is slipping. What can I do?</p>",
        "ggMtAgKquLF_childItem_9": "<p>Why is my baby able to knock off the footrest?</p>",
        "ggZY2ueO0on_text": "<p>Dangling legs are destabilizing and, for early eaters, can promote a slumping posture that increases choking risk. Your baby’s ability to rest his or her feet flat on a hard surface is key for promoting a safe swallow.&nbsp;</p>",
        "ggJUJAGgf6v_label": "<p>Read More</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_0": "<p>Kicking legs</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_1": "<p>Crossing ankles</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_2": "<p>Holding onto tray or armrest</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_3": "<p>Constant fidgeting and wobbling</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_4": "<p>Slouching to one side</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_5": "<p>Disinterest in food</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_6": "<p>Showing signs of hunger, but not finishing meals</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_7": "<p>Fussing throughout the meal</p>",
        "gg7qDCNyFLh_childItem_8": "<p>Resisting getting in the highchair or trying to escape</p>",
        "gg0n2yCEj-l_label": "<p>Read More</p>",
        "ggfCUdgaTGx_text": "<p>The 90/90/90 rule means your hips, knees and ankles should all be at 90° angles when eating. This position provides the most core (trunk) stability, which allows for controlled movement in the hands and mouth. Your feet need to rest on a flat, sturdy surface to achieve this ideal positioning.</p>",
        "ggZ_H9u-bvF_label": "<p>Read More</p>",
        "gg5uMmhUrw4_text": "<p>Yes, the footrest can be positioned high on the legs for little babies and moved down as they grow to keep the optimal 90/90/90 positioning. If your child is over one-year-old, we recommend adding the <a href=\"https://www.yeahbabygoods.com/collections/highchair-footrest/products/footrest-spacers-set-of-2\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><u>Footrest Spacer</u></strong></a> to keep the footrest from falling at a lower position.</p>",
        "ggx5IVPnqhN_text": "<p>All ages! Even adults crave a stable place to rest their feet. Picture sitting in a high stool with no foot support. You'd constantly be shifting, trying to get comfortable and stay balanced. Your attention stays on your body more than it should, which we especially don't want for babies who are still learning to eat!</p>",
        "ggE8Nx1fIhu_text": "<p>No tools needed! Just open the clamp's clasp, position it on the highchair's leg and snap it closed.&nbsp;</p>",
        "gg5Jvp-Sr5T_text": "<p>It's important to make sure the cut-outs are facing down and oriented correctly. One side of the cut-out is deeper than the other side. Make sure the<strong> side with the deeper cut is facing forward</strong> (closest to you if you're standing in front of the chair). You know it's right if the footrest lays flat and doesn't tilt back.&nbsp;</p>",
        "ggpuBsqFmih_label": "<p>Watch Installation Video</p>",
        "gg1muk0fgsW_text": "<p>The clamps can get stuck in the box, so please make sure to check both ends before throwing away the packaging. :)</p>",
        "gg1LiWis8TZ_text": "<p>We recommend first cleaning the legs with rubbing alcohol to see if natural oils from food or hands are causing it to slip. If that doesn't help, please <a href=\"https://www.yeahbabygoods.com/pages/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><u>contact us</u></strong></a> so we can help troubleshoot!</p>",
        "ggQWYcXox_Y_text": "<p>If the footrest is set low on the highchair legs, it can more easily slide out. Our <a href=\"https://www.yeahbabygoods.com/collections/highchair-footrest/products/footrest-spacers-set-of-2\" target=\"_blank\"><u>footrest spacers</u></a> keep the footrest from sliding back and forth and getting knocked off. If that doesn't seem to be the problem, just send a video to <a href=\"mailto:support@yeahbabygoods.com\">support@yeahbabygoods.com</a> and we'll help troubleshoot!</p>"
      }
    },
    "gp_section_633407305174221802": {
      "type": "gp-section-633407305174221802",
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "b13994e1bf07fa1f040e8a50881f4740ccbf7b970ca7d436a04b0574e35f50bd_1_1_1_0__1",
        "ggBSkNDlgts_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0306/4076/7108/files/baby-in-highchair-with-footrest-and-sage-placemat_8e1d4a91-bae2-415b-8687-4e14e6b2e762.jpg",
        "ggBSkNDlgts_alt": "Baby in IKEA Highchair with Yeah Baby Goods footrest and Sage placemat",
        "ggBSkNDlgts_title": "IKEA Highchair with YBG Accessories for Support and Comfort",
        "ggetBToYcnc_text": "Long, Peaceful Meals",
        "gg_zEFfcuQI_text": "<p>When babies' feet dangle without support, they expend a lot of energy just trying to stay stable. This leads to short, fussy meals. When a footrest is added, babies sit longer and show a greater interest in eating.&nbsp;</p>",
        "ggQoozfmIcb_text": "Improves Fine Motor Skills",
        "ggPGz24MFI0_text": "<p>Stable, comfortable babies can focus on the smaller muscles in their hands and mouth that control fine motor skills like grasping, pinching, hand-to-mouth coordination, biting, chewing and swallowing.&nbsp;</p>",
        "ggIecTy_s5I_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0306/4076/7108/files/girl-in-highchair-with-walnut-footrest.jpg",
        "ggIecTy_s5I_alt": "Child in ikea high chair with a tray placemat, using a dark wood footrest against a blue paneled wall",
        "ggIecTy_s5I_title": "Child in Highchair with Dark Wood Footrest",
        "ggVVeKAnDTS_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0306/4076/7108/files/child-in-highchair-with-cushion-placemat-footrest.jpg",
        "ggVVeKAnDTS_alt": "Child in an IKEA ANTILOP high chair with YBG cushion, footrest, and tray placemat in a home setting with wooden floor and furniture.",
        "ggVVeKAnDTS_title": "Title",
        "ggGOZORGXlr_text": "Decreases Choking Risk",
        "ggm0koQ_6n2_text": "<p>A lack of stability causes a slumping position that increases choking risk. Footrests help stabilize the core, which allows the swallow to work in a timely fashion, closing off the airway so liquid and food go right past the route to the lungs.</p>"
      }
    },
